    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50597" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴονθος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>root of a hair, young hair</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰόνθους ἐκθλιβομένους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Sign.</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Eun.
				<u>Hist.</u>
				p.250
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				<u>PS</u>
				p.77
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>eruption on the face, which often accompanies the first growth
				of the beard</i>, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				1.26
			</span></i>.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β́</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				556b29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pr.</u>
				963b40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλοφλυκτίδες</span>
			 :—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰονθώδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἐπάρσεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Sud.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.824
			</span></i>.</div>
